Author: Greg Detre <greg@gregdetre.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 3 06:17:18 2026 +0100

    261003e: GPT Sol's code-review fixes; focus indicators legible in Light
    
    - appearance.ts: a choice the browser refused to store is kept for the
      visit and no longer reverted by an OS change or bfcache restore; the
      control reads useAppearanceSaved() (Sol).
    - Dark is pixel-identical again: --destructive-button-foreground and
      --highlight-foreground (Sol).
    - Three logo animations use --highlight-text; scale tests measure against
      the real page tokens; stale dark-only comments fixed (Sol).
    - Focus indicators (left by Sol for me): --ring is --highlight-ink in
      Light, and 95 focus outlines, 11 accent-colors, 5 ring/outline utilities
      and 11 focus borders moved from the raw orange (~2.6:1 on the light page)
      to --highlight-text. Palette test pins --ring and --highlight-text at 3:1;
      the fixed-colours guard now rejects raw orange in outlines and accents.
    - The Google sign-in button uses Google's light palette in Light.
    - The browser check's screenshots, and the plan's record of both.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

