+1. **P1 — [src/web/appearance.ts:77](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbnv5bzx-light-dark-system/src/web/appearance.ts:77): an unsaved System choice could revert to the stored theme. Fixed.** When `localStorage.setItem()` failed, an OS-theme change or bfcache restore reread the older stored choice. The profile control could also retain a stale failure message after a cross-tab update. I separated storage refresh from applying current state, track page-only choices, and expose persistence through `useAppearanceSaved()`. [tests/appearance.test.ts:123](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbnv5bzx-light-dark-system/tests/appearance.test.ts:123) now exercises the actual radio control, hook snapshots, OS changes, bfcache, and cross-tab replacement.
+
+2. **P1 — [styles/tokens.css:179](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbnv5bzx-light-dark-system/styles/tokens.css:179): Light focus indicators and native control accents are below contrast requirements. Left for you.** `--ring` remains `#DB8A45`, about 2.6:1 against Light, below the 3:1 non-text threshold. The same affects 71 directly identifiable focus outlines among 94 raw-orange outline declarations, plus 10 real `accent-color` uses such as [AppearanceSetting.tsx:45](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbnv5bzx-light-dark-system/src/web/AppearanceSetting.tsx:45). The palette test does not cover `--ring`, while [web-client.md:401](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbnv5bzx-light-dark-system/docs/project/web-client.md:401) still describes it as 7.3:1. I left this because resolving it means choosing and documenting a theme-aware focus/control token across roughly 100 established declarations, contrary to the current rule that outlines stay raw orange.
+
+3. **P2 — [button.tsx:50](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbnv5bzx-light-dark-system/src/web/components/ui/button.tsx:50): Dark was no longer pixel-equivalent. Fixed.** The destructive button changed from white to off-white, while orange-filled controls changed from `--page` to `--primary-foreground`. I added theme-aware `--destructive-button-foreground` and `--highlight-foreground` tokens, preserving the previous Dark values while keeping Light legible. The affected Dock, profile microphone, and live-conversation controls now use them.
+
+4. **P2 — [logo-animations.css:545](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbnv5bzx-light-dark-system/src/web/styles/logo-animations.css:545): three orange text animations escaped the `--highlight-text` sweep. Fixed.** Strain, Dawn and Dew still used raw `--highlight`, producing 2.6:1 animated text in Light. They now use `--highlight-text`; [appearance-fixed-colours.test.ts:272](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbnv5bzx-light-dark-system/tests/appearance-fixed-colours.test.ts:272) now rejects future raw-orange CSS/Tailwind text.
+
+5. **P2 — [colour-scales.test.ts:60](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbnv5bzx-light-dark-system/tests/colour-scales.test.ts:60) and [hit-colours.test.ts:267](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbnv5bzx-light-dark-system/tests/hit-colours.test.ts:267): contrast tests used copied page values. Fixed.** Changing either theme’s real `--background` would not have changed the measured contrast. Both tests now parse the actual dark and light token blocks and fail if the page token disappears or changes adversely.
+
+6. **P2 — [styles.css:4](/home/greg/code/spideryarn2/.claude/worktrees/fbnv5bzx-light-dark-system/src/web/styles.css:4): several current comments and docs still described a dark-only app. Fixed.** I corrected the token, figure-sheet, gutter, logo-animation, design-page, original-version, logo, and historical browser-pass wording. The remaining false focus-ring wording is part of finding 2.
+
+Verdict: The before-paint ordering and resolution logic, Tailwind dark variant, feedback diagnostic fields and validation, palette block coverage, and hard-coded-colour allowlist otherwise look sound. The only unresolved release-significant issue is Light focus/control contrast. The focused suite passed: 8 files/283 tests plus 16 doc-link tests; the full typecheck passed all 2,782 source files via `node --import tsx scripts/typecheck.ts` (`npm run typecheck` itself could not start because this sandbox rejected tsx’s `/tmp` IPC socket). I did not run the full suite or commit, and left the existing untracked review/screenshot artifacts untouched.
